course: dictionary
lesson: 15747
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word tremor has three. You can work out which one is meant by reading the words around it. «The ground gave a tremor and the cups fell off the shelf.» The ground is shaking and cups are falling, so tremor must mean a small earthquake.
explain: «Grandpa's hand had a tremor, so he could not hold the pen steady.» The clues are hand and pen. A tremor here is a shaking in part of the body that you cannot control. Always ask which meaning fits the story, then try it in the sentence.
explain: «Her voice had a tremor when she said she was scared.» The clue is scared, a strong feeling. A tremor in the voice is a shake in how you speak, caused by fear or strong feelings. One word, three meanings: the context tells you which one to use.
fact: A tremor is a small earthquake, or a slight shaking of the ground.
fact: A tremor can also be a slight shaking of part of the body, such as the hands, that you cannot control.
fact: A tremor in the voice is a shake in how you speak, often from fear or strong feelings.
fact: Scientists measure tremors with a seismometer.
fact: An aftershock is a tremor that comes after a big earthquake.
exercise: «The ground gave a tremor and the cups fell off the shelf.» What does tremor mean here? | A loud song | A shake in the voice from fear | A cold drink | *A small earthquake
exercise: «Grandpa's hand had a tremor, so he could not hold the pen steady.» What does tremor mean here? | A small earthquake | A happy shout | A tall building | *A shaking in part of the body that you cannot control
exercise: «Her voice had a tremor when she said she was scared.» What does tremor mean here? | *A shake in the voice from fear | A bright light | A loud bang | A type of bird
test: «The scientists put a seismometer on the hill to catch every tremor.» What is a seismometer used for? | To make music | *To measure small earthquakes and tremors | To bake bread | To carry water
test: «After the big earthquake, there were several aftershocks.» What is an aftershock? | *A tremor that comes after a big earthquake | A loud bang at a football game | A large wave from the sea | A type of rain
exam: «Ella's voice gave a tremor as she read her poem aloud.» What does tremor mean here? | A tall building | *A shake in the voice from nerves | A sudden loud noise | A kind of bird
